[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Table of Contents
[/meta]

h1. Table of Contents

Tests for Section 18 of the specification.

h2. Basics

h3. All headings {#toc-basic}
[code om]
[toc]

h1. Guide
h2. Install
h2. Use
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#guide">Guide</a>
<ol>
<li><a href="#install">Install</a></li>
<li><a href="#use">Use</a></li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h1 id="guide">Guide</h1>
<h2 id="install">Install</h2>
<h2 id="use">Use</h2>
[/code]

h3. Level range {#toc-range}
[code om]
[toc 2-3]

h1. Guide
h2. Install
h3. Windows
h4. Details
h2. Use
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#install">Install</a>
<ol>
<li><a href="#windows">Windows</a></li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><a href="#use">Use</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h1 id="guide">Guide</h1>
<h2 id="install">Install</h2>
<h3 id="windows">Windows</h3>
<h4 id="details">Details</h4>
<h2 id="use">Use</h2>
[/code]

h3. Custom heading IDs are used in links {#toc-custom-id}
[code om]
[toc]

h2. Setup {#install}
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#install">Setup</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="install">Setup</h2>
[/code]

h2. Titles

h3. Title {#toc-title}
[code om]
[toc Contents]

h2. One
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">Contents</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#one">One</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="one">One</h2>
[/code]

h3. Range and title {#toc-range-title}
[code om]
[toc 2-4 Contents]

h1. Book
h2. Chapter
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">Contents</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#chapter">Chapter</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h1 id="book">Book</h1>
<h2 id="chapter">Chapter</h2>
[/code]

h3. A heading slug avoids the earlier table of contents ID {#toc-id-collision}
[code om]
[toc Contents]

h2. Toc 1
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">Contents</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#toc-1-2">Toc 1</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="toc-1-2">Toc 1</h2>
[/code]

h3. Untitled tables of contents do not use up IDs {#toc-id-untitled-skipped}
[code om]
[toc]

[toc Contents]

h2. One
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#one">One</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">Contents</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#one">One</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="one">One</h2>
[/code]

h3. Inline formatting in the title {#toc-title-formatting}
[code om]
[toc *Contents*]

h2. One
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1"><strong>Contents</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#one">One</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="one">One</h2>
[/code]

h3. A first word with letters is a title, not a range {#toc-title-not-range}
[code om]
[toc 2-hour guide]

h2. One
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">2-hour guide</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="#one">One</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="one">One</h2>
[/code]

h2. Matching Headings

h3. No headings, with a title {#toc-empty-titled}
[code om]
[toc Contents]

Just text.
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-1">
<p class="toc-title" id="toc-1">Contents</p>
</nav>
<p>Just text.</p>
[/code]

h3. No headings, without a title {#toc-empty-untitled}
[code om]
[toc]

Just text.
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc"></nav>
<p>Just text.</p>
[/code]

h3. No heading in the range {#toc-empty-range}
[code om]
[toc 3-4]

h2. Only level two
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc"></nav>
<h2 id="only-level-two">Only level two</h2>
[/code]

h3. Headings inside an expandable block count {#toc-inside-more}
[code om]
[toc]

[more Open]
h2. Hidden
[/more]
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#hidden">Hidden</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<details>
<summary>Open</summary>
<h2 id="hidden">Hidden</h2>
</details>
[/code]

h2. Hierarchy

h3. Skipped levels do not create empty items {#toc-skipped-levels}
[code om]
[toc]

h2. A
h4. B
h2. C
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#a">A</a>
<ol>
<li><a href="#b">B</a></li>
</ol>
</li>
<li><a href="#c">C</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="a">A</h2>
<h4 id="b">B</h4>
<h2 id="c">C</h2>
[/code]

h3. A deeper first heading stays at the top level {#toc-deeper-first}
[code om]
[toc]

h3. A
h2. B
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#a">A</a></li>
<li><a href="#b">B</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h3 id="a">A</h3>
<h2 id="b">B</h2>
[/code]

h2. Entry Text

h3. Inline formatting is kept {#toc-formatting}
[code om]
[toc]

h2. Using *bold* text
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#using-bold-text">Using <strong>bold</strong> text</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="using-bold-text">Using <strong>bold</strong> text</h2>
[/code]

h3. Links are reduced to their text {#toc-link-text}
[code om]
[toc]

h2. About [OireMark]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#about-oiremark">About OireMark</a></li>
</ol>
</nav>
<h2 id="about-oiremark">About <a href="https://example.com">OireMark</a></h2>
[/code]

h2. Errors

h3. Reversed range {#toc-range-reversed}
[code om]
[toc 4-2]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-toc-range 1
[/code]

h3. Level zero {#toc-range-zero}
[code om]
[toc 0-3]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-toc-range 1
[/code]

h3. Level seven {#toc-range-seven}
[code om]
[toc 2-7 Contents]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-toc-range 1
[/code]

h3. Table of contents mid-line {#toc-mid-line}
[code om]
See [toc]
[/code]
[code error]
block-tag-mid-line 1
[/code]

h3. Not allowed in the standard profile {#toc-profile-standard}
; profile
: standard
[code om]
[toc]
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 1
[/code]
